# Reference Point — Story Duo Solution Copy (`p.copy` in `.story-duo`)

When the user says **"reference point"** for canvas annotation design-solution copy (e.g. Trade Off side-by-side summary), match `p.copy` inside `.story-duo .side.is-solution`.

## Structure

```html
<aside class="to-annot-wrap" aria-label="Trade Off annotation">
  <div class="story-duo">
    <div class="side is-friction">
      <p class="label">User Friction</p>
      <p class="quote for-idle">Similar pieces look interchangeable — buyers can't tell what they're trading away.</p>
      <p class="quote for-open">A ₹74,500 gap reads as a discount — not as craft, weight, certification, and resale traded away.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="side is-solution">
      <p class="label">Design Solution</p>
      <p class="copy for-idle">Side-by-side comparison on price, technique, and weight — with an AI summary that makes the savings vs craft trade-off legible</p>
      <p class="copy for-open">Attribute rows plus an AI summary name what Celeste saves and what Mira keeps — so the trade-off is decideable, not guessed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <span class="to-annot-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</aside>
```

Use `.copy` on the **solution** side; use `.quote` on the **friction** side.

## Visual spec — `p.copy` (solution side)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Element | `p.copy` inside `.story-duo .side.is-solution` |
| Font | `var(--ui-sans)` |
| Size | `14px` |
| Weight | `500` |
| Color | `#6a6158` |
| Line-height | `1.45` |
| Width | `100%` |
| Margin | `0` |

## Story duo wrapper

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Wrapper | `.story-duo` |
| Layout | column flex, `gap: 16px`, `align-items: flex-start` |
| Accent | `padding-left: 12px`, `border-left: 1px solid rgba(162, 130, 90, 0.38)` |

## Side stack

| Side | Label color | Body class |
|------|-------------|------------|
| `.is-friction` | `var(--label)` | `.quote` — `16px`, `#3d3832`, weight 500 |
| `.is-solution` | `#849b89` (sage) | **`.copy`** ← this reference |

Labels: `11px`, weight 700, `0.14em` tracking, uppercase.

## Interactive states (Trade Off)

Pair idle/open copy on the same side:

| Class | When visible |
|-------|----------------|
| `.for-idle` | Default — sheet closed |
| `.for-open` | When parent `.to-feature.is-tradeoff-open` |

Toggle via `display: none` / `display: block`; both share the same `.copy` styling.

## vs other copy styles

| Class | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `p.copy` in `.story-duo .is-solution` | Canvas annotation design solution — compact UI sans, `#6a6158` |
| `p.copy` in `.cert-feature-foot` | Feature footer column — grey sans, `0.875rem`, `var(--muted)` |
| `.lead` in `.story-duo .is-solution` | Cert feature annotation (var-d) — grey sans, `var(--body)` |
| `.quote` in `.story-duo .is-friction` | Friction side — darker `#3d3832`, `16px` |

## Do not

- Use `.copy` on the friction side — use `.quote`.
- Match `.cert-feature-foot .copy` sizing here — annotation copy is `14px` / `#6a6158`, not `0.875rem` / `var(--muted)`.
- Remove `.for-idle` / `.for-open` when the annotation swaps on interaction.
